{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1550245-wings-as-a-part-of-characters-fae-mein","id":1550245,"title":"Wings as a part of characters Fae Mein","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-18T12:11:07-07:00","id":1550245,"title":"Wings as a part of characters Fae Mein","content":"I have a question regarding the addition of wings in the Fae mein of a changeling. I have noticed that the only kith that explicitly states the power of is the Draconic kith, and I have also noticed that in the description of the Riddleseeker Kith there is an example of a Beast/Riddleseeker that resembled a Sphynx from Greek mythology and its mein included a pair of wings. My question is what exactly are the mechanics for flight for any Changeling who has wings as an aspect of their fae mein when said wings are not explicitly stated as an option of the kith blessing? For example, Let's Say I decided I wanted to make a Darkling/Stoneflesh based on a Gargoyle and described him as having wings, what would be the rules I would use to have that character fly or glide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T19:06:54-07:00","id":1550255,"title":"","content":"If you don't have a mechanic that says you can fly, you do not have the ability to fly. Getting the ability to fly entails having something on your character sheet that provides that ability, whether it's a kith blessing, a Contract, a Token, some other Merit, a piece of equipment, or something else. Ditto for gliding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T06:28:46-07:00","id":1550263,"title":"","content":"Ok, can one gain wings by use of the fang and talon steed contract benefit of gaining the transportation method of a chosen animal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T06:32:18-07:00","id":1550264,"title":"","content":"That is the described effect of that Contract, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T07:04:09-07:00","id":1550267,"title":"","content":"In C:tD <b>Wings</b> were a four point merit if you wanted to fly. However, the flight power cut off if Banal people saw you. Although C:tL and C:tD are very different games, the mechanics should be easy to flip from one game to the next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T08:21:09-07:00","id":1550269,"title":"","content":"I have one other question about the fang and talon contract. Can a character use this contract to gain the tail of a fish or other aquatic transportation method as well as an ability to breathe water similar to the Swimmerskin kith benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T10:25:58-07:00","id":1550273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1550245-wings-as-a-part-of-characters-fae-mein?p=1550269#post1550269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one other question about the fang and talon contract. Can a character use this contract to gain the tail of a fish or other aquatic transportation method as well as an ability to breathe water similar to the Swimmerskin kith benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Water breathing is not one of the standard set of options for the Contract, so that would have to be part of a Seeming bonus or a Merit modifying the Contract. Increased swimming Speed would work as described in the first effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T13:39:43-07:00","id":1552548,"title":"","content":"In CtL 1e there were two Kiths that allowed limited flight: Airtouched took only minimal damage from falling, and Lurkgliders were capable of gliding (though not true flight). <br /> <br /> In Princess: The Hopeful 2e, there's an Umbra (Dread Power) called &quot;Night Raptor&quot; which allows true flight, though it's generally limited to NPCs. PCs can use the Charm &quot;Wings of Air (Perfect \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Aria \u2022\u2022\u2022)&quot;, which has some actual hard mechanics to determine how fast you can fly and how many passengers you can carry, of any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}